1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''"The five colonial Cilacap Regents all sprang in the direct male line from Tjakrawedana, while the Bupati of Purwokerto until 1924 were also from the Tjakrawedana line, as they stemmed from the Banyumas Tjokroneg
2 CONC oro. In '''1924''', '''R.T. Ario Tjokroadisoerjo''', a man of Ponorogo descent and brother-in-law of the nationalist leader, '''H.O.S. Tjokroaminoto''', was appointed and governed in Purwokerto until its abolition as a Regency in 
2 CONC '''1935'''. These three Regencies were thus ruled by a close-knit family with roots in the pre-colonial past. Until 1878, the Bupati of Banjarnegara were also linked to this family."''
2 CONT
2 CONT Taken from "Notes on Java's Regent Families: Part II" By : H Sutherland
